 "note": "Read from the cosmetic list's ext-data heap (one contiguous blob after the 664-byte descriptors, consumed in entry order, ImageListingEntrySize + OtherEntrySize per entry). Entries are selected by CosmeticTypeSymbol (+0x68), which -- like every symbol in this table -- is stored BYTE-REVERSED; selecting by internal-name prefix instead silently drops the `rwd_*` ones. \u26a0 The authored float32 are sRGB-ENCODED, not linear: `tint_neutral_m_default` (\"Black Hole\") authors 0.15/0.9, which as sRGB are #262626 and #e6e6e6 -- near-black and white, matching the game. Read as linear they become a washed-out mid-grey pair (#6c6c6c/#f3f3f3), which is how every tint ended up too weak. `*_linear` is the converted value a renderer wants; `*_hex` is the direct byte encoding. An emissive is ExtDataParamCount RGB float32 triples. The chassis emissive MAP is a zone MASK, not a colour image: its shipped red/green are DEFAULTS that the player's chosen emissive replaces, mask channel N taking colour N.",
